# Rosetta options for de novo free-glycan probe modeling
# (glycographer.model / scripts/model_glycan_probes.py).
#
# Identical to the flags the legacy scripts/glycomodeler.py generated
# internally, so new probe models stay comparable with the existing ones.

# Score with beta_nov16 during GlycanSampler minimization. NOTE: GlycanDock
# sampling (glycandock_stage_*.init) does NOT pass -beta, so probes are
# minimized under a different score function than they are later docked with.
# Kept for parity with every existing probe model; revisit deliberately (and
# remodel all probes together) rather than piecemeal.
-beta

-include_sugars
-auto_detect_glycan_connections
-alternate_3_letter_codes pdb_sugar
-maintain_links

# Write PDB 3-letter codes (NAG, GAL, SIA, ...) and LINK records, so the models
# read straight back into GlycanDock and so glycographer.model can check the
# written residue codes against the probe name.
-write_pdb_link_records
-write_glycan_pdb_codes

-ignore_unrecognized_res
-ignore_zero_occupancy false
-load_PDB_components false
-no_fconfig
